# Infrastructure Plan

## Overview

This document defines the planned infrastructure for the Enterprise Hybrid IT Lab. The environment will simulate a small enterprise with on-premises Windows Server infrastructure integrated with Microsoft Entra ID, Microsoft 365, Intune, PowerShell, and ServiceNow.

## Virtualization Platform

**Hypervisor:** VirtualBox

**Environment:** Hybrid on-premises and cloud

## Planned Infrastructure

| System   | Operating System         | Primary Role                           |
| -------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| DC01     | Windows Server 2019/2022 | Active Directory Domain Services + DNS |
| SRV01    | Windows Server 2019/2022 | DHCP + File Server                     |
| WIN11-01 | Windows 11               | Employee Workstation                   |
| WIN11-02 | Windows 11               | Employee Workstation                   |

## DC01 — Domain Controller

DC01 will serve as the primary domain controller for the environment.

### Responsibilities

* Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
* DNS
* Domain authentication
* User and computer account management
* Organizational Units
* Security Groups
* Group Policy

## SRV01 — Server

SRV01 will provide network and file services.

### Responsibilities

* DHCP
* Department file shares
* NTFS permissions
* Shared network resources

## Windows Workstations

### WIN11-01

* Windows 11
* Domain-joined employee workstation
* Managed through Group Policy
* Later managed through Microsoft Intune

### WIN11-02

* Windows 11
* Domain-joined employee workstation
* Used to test policies, permissions, and troubleshooting scenarios
* Later managed through Microsoft Intune

## Microsoft Entra ID

Microsoft Entra ID will provide cloud identity and access management.

### Planned Uses

* Cloud user management
* Cloud groups
* Authentication
* Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
* Hybrid identity

## Microsoft 365

Microsoft 365 will provide cloud productivity and collaboration services.

### Planned Services

* Exchange Online
* Microsoft Teams
* SharePoint
* OneDrive
* Microsoft 365 licensing

## Microsoft Intune

Intune will provide endpoint management for Windows devices.

### Planned Uses

* Windows device enrollment
* Configuration profiles
* Compliance policies
* Endpoint security policies
* Device inventory
* Application deployment

## PowerShell

PowerShell will be used to automate and administer the environment.

### Planned Uses

* Active Directory administration
* User creation
* User modification
* User offboarding
* Group management
* Reporting
* Troubleshooting
* Administrative automation

## ServiceNow

ServiceNow will provide IT service management capabilities.

### Planned Uses

* Incident management
* Service requests
* User onboarding
* User offboarding
* Assignment groups
* Ticket documentation
* IT service management workflows

## Planned Virtual Machine Resources

| VM       | CPU    | RAM  | Storage |
| -------- | ------ | ---- | ------- |
| DC01     | 2 vCPU | 4 GB | 60 GB   |
| SRV01    | 2 vCPU | 4 GB | 60 GB   |
| WIN11-01 | 2 vCPU | 6 GB | 64 GB   |
| WIN11-02 | 2 vCPU | 6 GB | 64 GB   |

These resource allocations are initial estimates and may be adjusted based on available host hardware.

## Infrastructure Dependencies

The infrastructure will be built in the following general order:

1. Windows Server infrastructure
2. Active Directory and DNS
3. DHCP and file services
4. Windows client deployment
5. Group Policy
6. PowerShell automation
7. Microsoft Entra ID
8. Hybrid identity
9. Microsoft 365
10. Microsoft Intune
11. ServiceNow
12. Enterprise troubleshooting scenarios

## Project Goal

The infrastructure will provide a realistic enterprise environment for practicing Windows Server administration, identity management, endpoint management, cloud integration, PowerShell automation, troubleshooting, security controls, and IT service management.
